    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0449" n="419" sameAs="frus:frus1949v01/pg419"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Policy Planning Staff Files<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d158-f1"/>
                </note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Report by the Policy Planning Staff</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-02-07">February 7, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"> PPS/48</p>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atomic Energy Policy vis-à-vis</hi> U.K. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">and Canada</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The two attached documents—the memorandum of February 3, 1949 and the notes of
                    January 28, 1949—are not Policy Planning Staff papers, but they were prepared
                    with the active participation of Messrs, Kennan<anchor n="3" xml:id="d158-f2"/>
                    and Butler.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d158-f3"/> Consequently, they have been given a
                    PPS number and included with the regular folders of Planning Staff papers.</p>



                <xi:include href="d158-a1.xml" xpointer="d158-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d158-a2.xml" xpointer="d158-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
